# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Canonical host is the bare apex, telaventis.fr (see every <link
# rel="canonical"> and sitemap.xml). This rule only does anything once
# www.telaventis.fr is ALSO added as a custom domain on the Pages project
# pointing here — until then it is simply inert. Once it is, this stops
# the site being reachable at two different hostnames at once, which
# search engines would otherwise treat as duplicate content and which
# gives a spoofer one more look-alike surface to register a lookalike TLS
# cert against and phish from.
https://www.telaventis.fr/* https://telaventis.fr/:splat 301!

# The authoring tools and their inputs (_outils/: identity generator, project
# data, capture scripts, source images) live in the repository so the site
# can be rebuilt from them, but they are not part of the site: never served.
/_outils/* /404.html 404
/_outils /404.html 404
/.claude/* /404.html 404
